# Afterglow film LUT (integrator). Display-encoded sRGB in -> out; the LUT slot after PBR Neutral, saturation,
# sRGB OETF and lift/gamma/gain (scene/src/core/final.js). Hand-built constrained grade, NOT a free fit:
#   OKLab chroma x k(L), k = s + (1-s)*smoothstep(L0, L1, L), hue and OKLab L kept (shadow desaturation);
#   above OKLab L = Lh: hue pulled toward peach #FEC08A by hp*ramp, chroma x (1 + hc*ramp), ramp = smoothstep(Lh, Lh+0.2, L).
# params {"s": 0.6, "L0": 0.14, "L1": 0.34, "hp": 0, "Lh": 0.6, "hc": 0.15, "gm": 0.98, "sh": 260.0, "shs": 0.0}
# gm (v2, fix round 4): the highlight chroma boost saturates smoothly below the chroma where a display channel reaches gm (no clipped lattice entries).
# fitted by sandbox/integration/lut/fit_grade.py on the stills that realise refs: sandbox/integration/lut/fit_v2.py (fix round 4, resumed 2026-10-23) on the out/v7 ungraded stills (integ5 = live modules 07:04; lut/wide_s_v7.json, lut/wide_s06_v7.json): the wides' ungraded dark chroma fell to 12.9-21.2 (integ2: 16.1-22.0), so s 0.5 left S05/S17 6.9 and S20 5.9 under the 7-12 target; s 0.6 (the look critic's value) puts 8 of 9 wides in 7-12 (S01 12.9, ref 16.0) and is closer to the refs' shadow chroma (mean |dc - ref| 2.7 vs 3.1)
# baked by: python sandbox/integration/lut/bake_lut.py sandbox\integration\lut\film_v3_wide.json --title afterglow film v3 wide --out sandbox\integration\lut\afterglow_film_wide_v3.cube
